<title>USA: Vermont urges aid program buy heating oil in bulk.</title>
<headline>Vermont urges aid program buy heating oil in bulk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Governor of Vermont proposed buying home heating oil in bulk for the Low Income Home Heating Assistance Program as a way of stretching the program's funds.</p>
<p>Governor Howard Dean said bulk purchases could capture discount prices, and help protect aid recipients from price fluctuations in the energy marketplace.</p>
<p>The Dean Administration said similar efforts in Boston and New York have saved as much as 15 percent of home heating oil costs.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
